      "message": "fix(post): the Fanuc lathe leaves a face-drilled hole at the stream's exit\n\nfanuc-lathe.cps swallowed every move after a face cycle (G83/G84/G85)\nuntil the section ended, so the chain's exit rapid up to clearance never\nposted: the tool left the hole at R and G28 U0 W0 moved X and Z together\nfrom below the verified path.\n\n#994's hop law now holds on the lathe: the cycle replaces only the chain\non its hole (on centre, at or below R); the first rapid leaving it ends\nthe group with G80 and posts as the stream says. A cut leaving the hole\ninside an open group is refused by name. tormach-lathe.cps posts the\nchain as plain moves and already exits at clearance; unchanged.\n\nPinned by lathe_cycle_exit (a read-back checker run on both lathe posts\nover the axial-drill document) and a synthetic stream in\nlathe_post_refusals. The fanuc-lathe axial_drill.nc golden gains the\nG00 X0 Z30 exit before G28 U0 W0.\n\nFixes #1011\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
